    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI made `householdId` a deterministic function of `(lastName, postcode)` and rewired everything that keys off the household to use it, keeping each piece of logic in its natural place.\n\n**`HouseholdIdGenerator`** \u2014 now hashes `normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode` and returns the first 12 hex chars of SHA-256 (lowercase, no prefix), per the spec. Returns `null` when there's no postcode, so an owner without one belongs to no shared household. It stays the single source of the id.\n\n**`Owner`** \u2014 added a request-scoped, non-persisted `@Transient declaredHouseholdMember` flag so the \"declared member is not a suspected duplicate\" rule can be expressed cleanly without polluting persistence or the API DTO.\n\n**`ClinicServiceImpl`**:\n- `saveOwner` now stamps every new owner's `householdId` from the generator (via a small `householdIdFor` helper), so household size and duplicate detection both read the same computed id.\n- `householdSizeIncluding` already keyed off `householdId`, and now benefits from it always being populated.\n- `findPossibleDuplicate` now keys off the computed `householdId` and returns empty for declared members \u2014 so a declared household member is never flagged.\n- Replaced the obsolete `existsOwnerByIdentityKey`/`shareHousehold`/`householdMembers` (the old \"create the link + backfill\" and identity-key duplicate block) with a single focused `isHouseholdOccupied(owner)`.\n\n**`ClinicService`** \u2014 interface updated to drop `shareHousehold`/`existsOwnerByIdentityKey` and add `isHouseholdOccupied`.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 `sharesHousehold` no longer creates a link; it only bypasses the new household-duplicate block. A second owner sharing `(lastName, postcode)` gets a 409 unless it sets `sharesHousehold`, in which case it's created as a declared member (flag passed through to `saveOwner`).\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `householdId`, `sharesHousehold`, `possibleDuplicate`, and `identityKey` descriptions/examples to match the new deterministic, postcode-keyed behaviour.\n\nNothing else referenced the removed methods, and the derived `identityKey` field remains available for API serialization.",
